Patch 0196: remove the per-game fast paths.

The core carried fast paths written for one commercial game's code layout,
at fixed guest addresses, on by default: an idle poll loop and a title loop
rewritten as host loops, five call-branch helpers, the OS interrupt routines
(OSDisable/Enable/RestoreInterrupts) matched at the address one game links
them, four wasm-JIT imports and the inline wasm calls to them, their
verify/read helpers, counters, stats-line segments and disassembler
printers, and a CoreTiming probe for one wedge address. All of it goes; a bl
to those addresses is now an ordinary call. Disable bits 0, 1 and 2 are left
unused. AOT_COMPILER_VERSION 37: block and region modules lose four imports.
Comments that named games now name the genre.

